  "limitations": [
    "Centres are projected physical pedestal footprints estimated from opposite visible ground corners, not the apparent centres of the human figures. The fourth rear ground corner is inferred by a parallelogram, approximately two-pixel visual uncertainty.",
    "anchor_image_px is the distinct foremost bottom pedestal corner for Y-sorting. All simple component polygons of one statue share that anchor.",
    "Attributes and the hanging cloak are separate simple component polygons so gaps remain transparent; contours come solely from the ash painting.",
    "Shadows remain explicitly named opaque RGB floor-connection patches, not physical translucent shadow masks. Moving a statue requires retouching its ground connection.",
    "Binary masks preserve the original pixels exactly. Antialiased edge pixels already contain mixed background colour, so reuse away from this scene may need edge cleanup.",
    "Clean-plate reconstruction is limited to selected cores and small soft transitions. All source pixels outside these supports and all authored geometric guides remain unchanged.",
    "Hidden geometric guides are before-painting references. Their native dimensions are documented by the packager; they are not exact final-painting registration."
  ]
